ack decision quality evidence, which is a gap. We need to decide whether to shift recommendation.\n\nGiven the new evidence: C keeps calm in crisis (stress resilience) and makes correct decisions quickly (decision quality). B lacks decision quality evidence. So C may be stronger on critical safety criteria. However C's communication difficulty and egocentric may affect crew cooperation. But B also has pretentiousness and wrong tone, plus weak memory for numbers and nasty remarks. Both have communication concerns. C also has concern for others (positive). So perhaps C is now the stronger candidate.\n\nThus we can change vote to Candidate C, explaining that new evidence about C's stress resilience and decision quality addresses key safety criteria that B lacks, and that C's concern for others offsets communication issues.\n\nWe should reference earlier discussion: Agent 1 and 2 recommended B, but we now have evidence that C has stress resilience and decision quality, which are crucial. So we shift recommendation to C.\n\nProvide explicit facts: C keeps calm in a crisis, makes correct decisions quickly, excellent attention skills, puts concern for others above everything. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Compare to B's unknown decision quality, communication issues, weak memory for numbers. Argue that C's strengths in decision quality and stress resilience outweigh B's unknowns, and that his concern for others may mitigate crew cooperation issues.\n\nThus vote for Candidate C.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
